# Modular Healthcare Patient Monitoring System in C#

Below is a complete implementation of a modular healthcare patient monitoring system with three isolated layers as you requested. The system uses C# with clear separation of concerns between the layers.

## System Architecture

```
PatientMonitoringSystem/
├── Models/                  # Shared data models
├── Services/                # Core services
│   ├── VitalSignsIngester.cs
│   ├── AnomalyDetectionEngine.cs
│   └── EmergencyDispatch.cs
├── Repositories/            # Data storage interfaces
└── Program.cs               # Entry point
```

## Implementation

### 1. Models (Shared Data Models)

```csharp
// Models/VitalSign.cs
namespace PatientMonitoringSystem.Models
{
    public class VitalSign
    {
        public DateTime Timestamp { get; set; }
        public double HeartRate { get; set; } // in bpm
        public double SpO2 { get; set; }      // in percentage
    }
}
```

### 2. Vital Signs Ingester

```csharp
// Services/VitalSignsIngester.cs
using PatientMonitoringSystem.Models;
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

namespace PatientMonitoringSystem.Services
{
    public class VitalSignsIngester
    {
        private readonly List<VitalSign> _vitalSigns = new List<VitalSign>();
        private readonly object _lock = new object();

        public event Action<VitalSign> VitalSignReceived;

        public void SimulateTelemetryStream()
        {
            // Simulate receiving telemetry data from a device
            Random random = new Random();
            DateTime lastTime = DateTime.Now;

            while (true)
            {
                // Simulate new data every 5-15 seconds
                int delay = random.Next(5000, 15000);
                Task.Delay(delay).Wait();

                DateTime now = DateTime.Now;
                double heartRate = 60 + random.NextDouble() * 50; // 60-110 bpm
                double spo2 = 90 + random.NextDouble() * 20;      // 90-110%

                var sign = new VitalSign
                {
                    Timestamp = now,
                    HeartRate = Math.Round(heartRate, 1),
                    SpO2 = Math.Round(spo2, 1)
                };

                lock (_lock)
                {
                    _vitalSigns.Add(sign);
                }

                VitalSignReceived?.Invoke(sign);
            }
        }

        public IEnumerable<VitalSign> GetRecentSigns(int count)
        {
            lock (_lock)
            {
                return _vitalSigns.AsEnumerable()
                    .OrderByDescending(s => s.Timestamp)
                    .Take(count);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### 3. Anomaly Detection Engine

```csharp
// Services/AnomalyDetectionEngine.cs
using PatientMonitoringSystem.Models;
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

namespace PatientMonitoringSystem.Services
{
    public class AnomalyDetectionEngine
    {
        private readonly VitalSignsIngester _ingester;
        private readonly int _windowSize = 10; // Number of data points in sliding window
        private readonly double _heartRateThreshold = 120; // bpm
        private readonly double _spo2Threshold = 85; // percentage

        public event Action<string> AnomalyDetected;

        public AnomalyDetectionEngine(VitalSignsIngester ingester)
        {
            _ingester = ingester;
            _ingester.VitalSignReceived += ProcessVitalSign;
        }

        private void ProcessVitalSign(VitalSign sign)
        {
            var recentSigns = _ingester.GetRecentSigns(_windowSize);

            // Calculate moving averages
            double avgHeartRate = recentSigns.Average(s => s.HeartRate);
            double avgSpO2 = recentSigns.Average(s => s.SpO2);

            // Check for anomalies
            if (sign.HeartRate > _heartRateThreshold || avgHeartRate > _heartRateThreshold)
            {
                AnomalyDetected?.Invoke($"High heart rate detected: {sign.HeartRate} bpm (threshold: {_heartRateThreshold})");
            }

            if (sign.SpO2 < _spo2Threshold || avgSpO2 < _spo2Threshold)
            {
                AnomalyDetected?.Invoke($"Low SpO2 detected: {sign.SpO2}% (threshold: {_spo2Threshold}%)");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### 4. Emergency Dispatch Subsystem

```csharp
// Services/EmergencyDispatch.cs
using System;
using System.Net.Mail;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

namespace PatientMonitoringSystem.Services
{
    public class EmergencyDispatch
    {
        private readonly string _adminEmail;
        private readonly string _adminPhone;

        public EmergencyDispatch(string adminEmail, string adminPhone)
        {
            _adminEmail = adminEmail;
            _adminPhone = adminPhone;
        }

        public async Task DispatchEmergency(string message)
        {
            // Send email notification
            await SendEmailNotification(message);

            // In a real system, you would also send SMS here
            // await SendSmsNotification(message);
        }

        private async Task SendEmailNotification(string message)
        {
            try
            {
                using (var smtpClient = new SmtpClient("smtp.example.com"))
                {
                    var mailMessage = new MailMessage
                    {
                        From = new MailAddress("monitoring@healthcare.com"),
                        Subject = "PATIENT EMERGENCY ALERT",
                        Body = $"ALERT: {message}\n\nPlease respond immediately.",
                        IsBodyHtml = false
                    };
                    mailMessage.To.Add(_adminEmail);

                    await smtpClient.SendMailAsync(mailMessage);
                }
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Failed to send email: {ex.Message}");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### 5. Main Program

```csharp
// Program.cs
using PatientMonitoringSystem.Services;
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

class Program
{
    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Initialize components
        var ingester = new VitalSignsIngester();
        var anomalyDetector = new AnomalyDetectionEngine(ingester);
        var dispatch = new EmergencyDispatch("admin@healthcare.com", "+1234567890");

        // Connect the emergency dispatch to anomaly detection
        anomalyDetector.AnomalyDetected += async (message) =>
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"ALERT: {message}");
            await dispatch.DispatchEmergency(message);
        };

        // Start the telemetry simulation
        Console.WriteLine("Starting patient monitoring system...");
        Console.WriteLine("Press any key to stop the simulation...");

        ingester.SimulateTelemetryStream();

        Console.ReadKey();
    }
}
```

## Key Features

1. **Modular Design**:
   - Each layer has a single responsibility
   - Clear interfaces between components
   - Easy to extend or replace individual components

2. **Anomaly Detection**:
   - Uses sliding window technique (10 most recent readings)
   - Detects both instantaneous and moving average anomalies
   - Configurable thresholds for heart rate and SpO2

3. **Emergency Dispatch**:
   - Supports email notifications (SMS would be added in production)
   - Asynchronous operation for non-blocking alerts

4. **Thread Safety**:
   - Proper locking for shared data in the ingester
   - Event-based communication between components

